+Reading: glue alone is the gain (+6% short, +3.5% at 54K); proj alone +1.5%, but on top of glue nothing measurable
+(glue already removed the quantize launches; what the multi kernel saves in launches it loses in its own run time);
+moe and wo are at best neutral (-1% / 0%). Recommended production setting: `LLAMA_INKLING_MK_GLUE=1` only, MK_PROJ
+optional. MK_MOE and MK_WO stay as switches but should not be built on.
+
+### Per-kernel times (nsys, CUPTI activity, self-test cases under replayed CUDA graphs; ncu needs a host driver setting)
+| kernel | time | bytes | bandwidth |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `mul_mat_vec_q<Q8_0>` 2304 x 3072 (one projection) | 12.2-14.3 us | 7.5 MB | 525-615 GB/s (56-66% of 936) |
+| `mul_mat_vec_q<Q8_0>` 2304 x 384 (R) | 3.2 us | 0.94 MB | 294 GB/s |
+| `mul_mat_vec_q_multi<Q8_0>` the 5 projections (8576 rows) | 35.2 us (vs 5 x 7.8 = 39) | 21 MB | 600 GB/s |
+| `mul_mat_vec_q<NVFP4>` gate_up, 8 experts x 2304 x 2304 | 31.7 us | 23.9 MB | 754 GB/s (80%) |
+| `mul_mat_vec_q_multi<NVFP4>` same (MK_MOE) | 32.8 us | | the 3.5% behind the bench shows |
+| glue kernel A (3 x CTRL_DOWN, 48 blocks) | 8.0 us | 3.5 MB | 440 GB/s |
+| glue kernel B (3 x CTRL_OUT rows + last-block norm/q8_1) | 11.9 us | 3.5 MB + tail | |
+| cooperative glue (A + B in one) | 25.0 us | | the glue2 loss |
+| the unfused loop-pass chain it replaces (per instance) | ~95 us of kernel time in 25 launches | | |
+| `rms_norm_f32`, `k_bin_bcast`, `concat`, `quantize_q8_1`, `unary tanh` | 1.2-2.2 us each | | launch-bound |
+
+So the expert products are bandwidth-bound already (80%); the attention projections run at 56-66% (the 3072-row Q8_0
+kernels) and 31% (the 384-row R); the glue kernels are latency-bound (few blocks) but replace 25 launches each. With
+graphs on a launch costs ~1.5-2 us on this GPU: glue removed ~314 launches for +5.5 tok/s (0.6 ms), i.e. ~1.9 us per
+launch, and the remaining ~2080 launches of the decode graph stand for ~3.5-4 ms of the 10.5 ms per token.
+
+### Where the next gains are (ranked by expected gain per effort)
+1. The layer-application kernel (iteration 7 design, now testable on the GPU host with MK_CHECK-style shadows per
+   phase): -1900 launches = -3 to -3.5 ms of 10.5 -> ~+35-45%. Weeks, not days; the glue is its first phase and the
+   mechanisms it needs (ticket pattern, scratch hand-off, device-function bodies) are proven bit-exact now.
+2. Glue + the 5 projections + the sinks/tap products in one launch per layer application (the first step of 1):
+   ~6-8 launches less per application (~350/token, ~0.6 ms, +5-6%); the multi body refactored into a virtual-block
+   device function (its bits depend on nwarps x rows_per_block per type). Pays for itself and de-risks 1.
+3. Projection bandwidth: a Q8_0/Q6_K GEMV tuned for 2304-wide rows at 85% of peak would save ~10 us per layer
+   application (~0.5 ms, +4-5%); independent of the launch work, bit-exactness would need the same reduction order
+   as mmvq (or a documented bound).
+Not worth more work: MK_MOE (parity in launches, kernel 3-8% slower), MK_WO (neutral), MK_GLUE=2 (slower than =1),
+multi-stream (no gain: the graph is a dependency chain).
